question:
Given the CSS below, what color will the paragraph display?
```css
p { color: blue; }
p { color: red; }
```

What will be the computed `font-size` of the child element?
```css
.parent { font-size: 16px; }
.child { font-size: 1.5em; }
```

How will the browser interpret this CSS rule?
```css
.box {
  width: 100px !important;
  width: 200px;
}
```

What will be the margin of this element after browser reflow?
```css
.box {
  margin: 20px;
  margin: unset;
}
```

Which CSS custom property will be resolved?
```css
:root { --color: red; }
.box { --color: blue; color: var(--color, green); }
```

What happens when you apply --webkit-transform in a browser that doesn't need the prefix?
```css
.box {
  -webkit-transform: rotate(45deg);
  transform: rotate(45deg);
}
```

In this nested rule context, which color will apply?
```css
.parent { color: red; }
.parent .child { color: inherit; }
```
